<title>GERMANY: Waigel says convergence to determine EMU schedule.</title>
<headline>Waigel says convergence to determine EMU schedule.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Monday the convergence criteria for Europe's Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) would determine the time plan for a single European currency.</p>
<p>Waigel told reporters a single currency would come when convergence is reached.  </p>
<p>European member states that meet the Maastricht criteria for EMU will adopt a single currency in 1999.</p>
<p>To qualify for EMU, members states must aim to ensure budget deficits in 1997 do not exceed three percent of gross domestic product and total public debt not more than 60 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
